<title>POLAND: POLISH AUG C/A SURPLUS $58 MLN, JAN-AUG $48 MLN.</title>
<headline>POLISH AUG C/A SURPLUS $58 MLN, JAN-AUG $48 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland had a current account</p>
<p>surplus of $58 million in August, after a $262 million surplus</p>
<p>in July, bringing the surplus in the January-August period to</p>
<p>$48 million, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p> POLISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	   AUG 1996   JULY 1996    AUG 95</p>
<p> current account mln USD		58	  262	   555</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	  -810	 -540	  -185</p>
<p> exports				 1,906	2,304	 2,061</p>
<p> imports				 2,716	2,844	 2,246</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	  703	  698	   753</p>
<p>					   JAN-AUG 1996    JAN-AUG 1995</p>
<p> current account mln USD		  48		 3,770</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	  -4,496		  -713</p>
<p> exports				  15,621		14,736</p>
<p> imports				  20,117		15,449</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	  4,898		 4,871</p>
<p>NOTE: From January 1996 the central bank introduced a new</p>
<p>category, &quot;unclassified flows&quot; which encompasses mainly</p>
<p>cross-border, unregistered trade flows.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
